{"name":"Rusty Gate","hex":"#af6649","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rusty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Marked or corroded by rust. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of the rust color, reddish or reddish-brown."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gun or in particular an old or worn one."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rusty"},{"term":"gate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A doorlike structure outside a house.","A doorway, opening, or passage in a fence or wall."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To keep something inside by means of a closed gate.","To punish (a student) by not allowing to leave the college grounds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gate","blocks":[{"text":"A gate or gateway is a point of entry to or from a space enclosed by walls or other barriers. The word is derived from Proto-Germanic *gatan, meaning an opening or passageway. Synonyms include portal. The concept originally referred to the gap or hole in the wall or fence, rather than a barrier which closed it. Gates may prevent or control the entry or exit of individuals, or they may be merely decorative. The moving part or parts of a gateway may be considered \"doors\", as they are fixed at one side whilst opening and closing like one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg/330px-Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gate"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f